This repository contains Python turtle code written by the author to
hand-reproduce the Microsoft 2012 four-color Logo for personal study.

IMPORTANT: There are two separate things here, with different owners.

1. THE CODE (turtle drawing logic in weiruan.pyw)
   Written by the repository author, and released under the MIT License
   below. You may use, copy, modify, and distribute this CODE freely,
   subject to the MIT terms.

2. THE MICROSOFT LOGO (the visual artwork the code draws)
   The Microsoft name, the four-color square design, and all related
   trademarks and trade dress are the exclusive property of
   Microsoft Corporation. They are NOT licensed to you by this
   repository. Running the code produces an image of a Microsoft
   trademark; that image remains subject to Microsoft's trademark rights
   and this project does not grant any right to use it for any
   commercial, public, or confusing purpose.

If Microsoft Corporation requests adjustment, renaming, or takedown,
the author will comply immediately.

